Correcting a note that was itself wrong

An earlier version of this note claimed the other ~66 files in this commit were Biome
reformatting and carried no behaviour change. That was wrong, and it was asserted
without checking: `git diff -w --ignore-blank-lines <parent> c7a945618 -- <file>` says
otherwise.

The real split of these 73 files:

  4 format-only:
    apps/vscode/src/core/storage/documents-path.ts
    apps/vscode/src/services/diagnostics/diagnostic-export.ts
    apps/vscode/src/shared/media.ts
    apps/vscode/src/shared/provider-performance.ts

  69 substantive, including:
    WebviewProvider.ts            +62
    webviewLoadGuard.test.ts      +76   (new)
    VscodeWebviewProvider.ts      +50
    FileLockManager.ts            +27 / -42
    WebviewMessage.ts             +18
    mentions/index.ts             +13 / -8
    settingsLock.ts                +2 / -12

So this commit is a real change spanning webview error reporting, file locking, MCP
and mentions - not one fix plus formatting noise. A history rewrite to "clean up 66
files of churn" would have rewritten 28 commits to remove 4 files' worth of
reformatting, which is a bad trade against the risk of a shared-branch force push.

The one lesson worth keeping from the wrong version: the per-file diff is the evidence,
and running it takes seconds. Not running it is how a confident, wrong claim about
someone else's commit gets written down.

Not cleaned up, and now not worth cleaning up. The 4 format-only files are harmless.
